findings.resolution:
RULE FOUND AND CENSUSED (2026-08-15); implementation is a JUDGE RIDER awaiting the user, because the population lives inside audit.py's money-box assertion and no producer change can close it alone (proven: the first attempt did exactly that and audit refused all five cells as 'enclosed empty box, no input').

THE RULE, reached by refuting three weaker ones in order:
  * row-local width alone (a cell narrower than an adjacent comb's slot) -- flips 5, but MISSES 1604CF's separators, which are 12.2-13.7pt, as wide as a character cell;
  * 'has decorative fill' -- 2,061 boxes are >=95% fill-covered and legitimately demand inputs (money boxes on tinted paper), so this is catastrophic;
  * 'dedicated fill' (a fill whose own rectangle is the cell's, within 1pt) -- 1,619 cells, almost all WHITE knockouts, i.e. the writing surfaces cut out of grey bands;
  * 'dedicated NON-WHITE fill' -- 8 cells, but 2 of them (2200AN p2c247/p2c255, 57.72pt wide, gray 0.9489) are schedule-table data cells that look writable by eye, not decoration.

What discriminates exactly is DEDICATED NON-WHITE FILL **AND FLANKED BY COMBS IN ITS OWN ROW**: 6 cells corpus-wide, every one a TIN group separator, nothing else. 2553-1999 p1c19/p1c21/p1c23 (peach, rgb 1.0/0.8/0.6, 4.5-4.8pt) and 1604cf-2008 p1c8/p1c10/p1c12 (grey 0.8902, 12.2-13.7pt) -- verified by eye at 300 dpi on both forms. The colour is not the signal and the width is not the signal; the signal is a decoration drawn FOR a cell that sits BETWEEN two character combs.

STILL OPEN, and the remaining scope is: 2553 p1c86 and 2551m p1c81 (1.54pt WHITE slivers between a comb2 and a comb4 in a date row -- no fill of their own, so this rule does not reach them) and 1701ms p1c51 (1.27pt, no comb neighbour at all). Three mechanisms, and only the first is solved.

FIXED (2026-08-15, user-approved package 71174630): PrintedDecoration in emit.py + the decoration rider in audit.py's money check. Flip census: corpus inputs 45,708 -> 45,700, exactly the 6 separators + F237's two cells, nothing else; 53/53 forms pass every audit assertion; all three rider clauses individually neuter-proven and a sub-glyph fixture added. The 2 white 1.54pt date slivers and 1701ms p1c51 were measured OUT of this rule's scope and remain tracked as minor residue in this finding's history -- they carry inputs that cannot fit a glyph and sit in no decorated cell; a later diagnosis owns them.
